# Dependency-free HTML report remains available if R Markdown is unavailable.
escape <- function(x) {x<-gsub('&','&amp;',as.character(x),fixed=TRUE);x<-gsub('<','&lt;',x,fixed=TRUE);gsub('>','&gt;',x,fixed=TRUE)}
html_table <- function(d) {for(v in names(d)) if(is.numeric(d[[v]])) d[[v]]<-signif(d[[v]],4); paste0('<table><thead><tr>',paste0('<th>',escape(names(d)),'</th>',collapse=''),'</tr></thead><tbody>',paste(vapply(seq_len(nrow(d)),function(i)paste0('<tr>',paste0('<td>',escape(unlist(d[i,])),'</td>',collapse=''),'</tr>'),character(1)),collapse=''),'</tbody></table>')}
sections <- c('<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Survival and Prognostic Factor Analysis in Clinical Trials</title><style>body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;line-height:1.55;color:#222}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;width:100%;margin:20px 0}th,td{padding:7px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left}th{background:#edf3f6}img{max-width:100%}h1,h2{color:#153c55}</style></head><body>',
 '<h1>Survival and Prognostic Factor Analysis in Clinical Trials</h1><p>Reproducible educational secondary analysis of survival::colon. Historical treatment assignments are not current clinical recommendations.</p>',
 '<h2>Clinical endpoints and analysis population</h2><p>The primary endpoint is all-cause death (etype=2), with status=1 indicating death and status=0 right censoring. Each patient contributes once. Time is recorded in days; plots use 365.25 days per year. The dataset does not provide enough metadata to independently verify every aspect of the trial time origin; registration is the working interpretation.</p>',
 '<p>The exploratory recurrence-or-death endpoint uses the earliest paired follow-up time and an event only if recurrence or death is observed at that time. Follow-up is conservatively censored at the shorter endpoint window. This reconstructed composite is not a verified protocol-defined DFS endpoint. Recurrence-only Kaplan-Meier is not interpreted as cumulative recurrence incidence in the presence of competing death.</p>',
 html_table(read.csv('results/tables/endpoints.csv')),html_table(read.csv('results/tables/cohort_flow.csv')),
 '<h2>Methods</h2><p>Unadjusted OS Kaplan-Meier estimates use log-log 95% confidence intervals; the global log-rank test compares three randomized groups. Pairwise tests are secondary and Holm-adjusted. The adjusted Cox model uses Efron ties and complete cases, with prespecified treatment, age per 10 years, log(1 + positive nodes), sex, obstruction, perforation, adherence, differentiation, local extent and surgery-to-registration category. No stepwise selection is used. node4 is excluded because documentation identifies discrepancies with nodes.</p>',
 '<p>Exponential, Weibull, log-normal and log-logistic AFT models use the identical complete-case cohort and covariates. AIC/BIC compare these likelihood-based models with each other; Cox partial-likelihood AIC is not compared with AFT AIC. AFT time ratios differ from Cox hazard ratios; the intercept is not a covariate time ratio. Standardized curves average predictions over observed covariates and have no uncertainty bands.</p>',
 '<h2>Baseline characteristics</h2>',html_table(read.csv('results/tables/baseline.csv')),
 '<h2>Overall survival</h2>','<img src="figures/km_overall_survival.png" alt="Overall survival and risk table">',
 html_table(read.csv('results/tables/logrank.csv')),html_table(read.csv('results/tables/km_landmarks.csv')),
 '<h2>Treatment effects and prognostic associations</h2>',html_table(read.csv('results/tables/cox_unadjusted.csv')),html_table(read.csv('results/tables/cox_adjusted.csv')),
 '<img src="figures/cox_forest.png" alt="Adjusted hazard ratios">',
 '<p>HR &lt; 1 indicates a lower instantaneous death hazard relative to the reference level, conditional on model covariates and proportional hazards. Randomized-treatment contrasts have a stronger causal basis than patient-characteristic associations, but complete-case exclusions and model assumptions limit causal interpretation. Prognostic associations do not establish causality or validated individual risk prediction.</p>',
 '<h2>Diagnostics and sensitivity analyses</h2>',html_table(read.csv('results/tables/proportional_hazards.csv')),
 sprintf('<p>The global PH test yields p=%.4g. Obstruction and differentiation show evidence against PH, so the common-HR model requires caution. A diagnostic-driven exploratory model stratifies baseline hazards by these factors; it retains treatment estimates but does not estimate their common prognostic HRs. Log-normal has the lowest candidate AFT AIC (%.2f).</p>',ph$table['GLOBAL','p'],min(comparison$AIC)),
 html_table(read.csv('results/tables/cox_ph_covariate_stratified.csv')),
 '<p>Schoenfeld tests and plots assess proportional hazards; a large p-value does not prove the assumption. Examine term-specific and global results together. The prespecified two-year treatment interaction and treatment-stratified model are exploratory sensitivity analyses; the latter has no common treatment HR. Martingale smooths and spline comparisons assess continuous-variable functional form. DFBETAS flags prompt review rather than automatic removal. Apparent concordance is not externally validated performance.</p>',
 '<img src="figures/schoenfeld.png" alt="Schoenfeld diagnostics"><img src="figures/martingale.png" alt="Functional form diagnostics"><img src="figures/influence.png" alt="Influence diagnostics">',
 html_table(read.csv('results/tables/functional_form_aic.csv')),html_table(read.csv('results/tables/cox_time_interaction.csv')),
 '<h2>Parametric models</h2>',html_table(comparison),html_table(aft_table),
 '<img src="figures/parametric_survival.png" alt="Standardized parametric survival"><img src="figures/aft_cox_snell.png" alt="Cox-Snell diagnostics">',
 '<p>Lower AIC reflects relative fit among the candidate models, not proof of correct tails or clinical validity. Inspect Cox-Snell departures and avoid unsupported extrapolation beyond observed follow-up. Confidence intervals are pointwise model-based intervals; this project does not make multiplicity-adjusted prognostic claims.</p>',
 '<h2>Exploratory composite endpoint</h2><img src="figures/km_recurrence_or_death.png" alt="Reconstructed composite endpoint">',
 '<h2>Limitations</h2><p>Historical public trial data; unavailable protocol metadata and modern biomarkers; missing covariates handled by complete-case analysis rather than imputation; sparse categories; noninformative censoring assumptions; known node-field inconsistencies; multiple exploratory analyses; no external validation. Results should be interpreted as an educational secondary analysis, not a confirmatory trial reanalysis or a clinical prediction tool.</p>',
 '<h2>Sources and reproducibility</h2><p><a href="https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/survival/html/colon.html">Official colon documentation</a>; <a href="https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/survival/html/survreg.html">survreg documentation</a>. See sessionInfo.txt, manifest.csv and validation.txt. CSV tables retain full precision; display formatting is handled by the R Markdown report.</p></body></html>')
writeLines(sections,'results/report.html')
